With this git repo the simulations and figures from Kronziel et al. "Improving Random Forest Interpretability with Clustering-Based Ensembles of Artificial Representative Trees" can be reproduced. Please note that the simulations in the paper were performed using a high-throughput batch system. Running the full calculations on your local system may take considerably longer.

To start, please open 01run_simulation_study.R in RStudio. Running this script generates the results and fitted ensembles for the main simulation study in the proc folder. The reduced default settings are intended to run in around five minutes, depending on your system. The original settings are included as comments in the script.

The scripts 02figure1.R, 02figure2.R, 02figure3.R, 02figureA1.R and 02figureA2.R can be used to reproduce Figures 1–3, A1 and A2 from the paper. By default, they use the results generated by the main simulation script. Figure A2 also uses the fitted ensembles. To use the precalculated paper results in the proc folder, comment out the block that loads the locally generated results in each figure script. For Figure A2, comment out the entire local loading block for both the results and the fitted ensembles.

To run the simulation sensitivity analyses, open 03run_simulation_sensitivity_analysis.R in RStudio. The default settings are reduced for local execution. The original settings are included as comments. Use 04figureA3.R for the variable selection comparison and 04figureA4.R for the clustering comparison. Both scripts use the results and fitted ensembles generated by the sensitivity analysis script. Please contact the authors to request the sensitivity analysis results used in the paper.

For any issues or questions please contact me by l.kronziel[at]uni-luebeck.de.
